      ],
      "section": "opening",
      "slot": "opening",
      "text": "Aspose.3D FOSS for Java is a free, open-source, MIT-licensed Java library for building and inspecting 3D scenes. It reads .stl, .fbx, .glb, .gltf, and .obj files and writes .stl, .fbx, .glb, .gltf, and .obj files. It exposes the same com.aspose.threed.* package, method signatures, and class names around a scene graph for organizing cameras and transforms as the commercial library. It requires Java 21 or later and has no required third-party package dependencies."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:com",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:1",
      "text": "Build a 3D scene graph with Scene, Node, and Entity, attaching geometry through Node.addEntity or Node.createChildNode and organizing it into a parent-child hierarchy."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "format:input.stl",
        "format:output.stl"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:2",
      "text": "Import and export STL geometry (binary or ASCII) with StlLoadOptions or StlSaveOptions, dispatched through Scene.fromFile or Scene.save."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "format:input.fbx",
        "format:input.glb",
        "format:input.gltf",
        "format:input.obj",
        "format:input.stl",
        "format:output.fbx",
        "format:output.glb",
        "format:output.gltf",
        "format:output.obj",
        "format:output.stl"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:3",
      "text": "Detect a 3D file's format automatically, or resolve an explicit format from a file path or binary stream using FileFormat.detect or FileFormat.getFormatByExtension."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:com",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:4",
      "text": "Generate primitive solids as ready-to-use geometry — Box, Cylinder, Sphere, and Dish each implement toMesh to produce a Mesh — and IFC-style 2D profiles such as CircleShape and EllipseShape."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:com",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:5",
      "text": "Define materials with LambertMaterial, PhongMaterial, and PbrMaterial — albedo, metallic/roughness, occlusion, and emissive channels, plus texture references — and assign them per node via Node.setMaterial."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:com",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:6",
      "text": "Model NURBS curves through NurbsCurve, exposing control points, knot vectors, and degree/order data."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "public_symbol:com",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "key_capabilities",
      "slot": "capability:7",
      "text": "Work with the transform and geometry math that underlies every scene operation — Vector2, Vector3, Vector4, Matrix4, Quaternion, and BoundingBox."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "identity:repository",
        "inherited_unit:047.paragraph",
        "public_symbol:com",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "intro",
      "text": "Aspose.3D FOSS for Java provides the Scene class as its central entry point, offering Scene.fromFile and Scene.save for automatic format detection and export. The com.aspose.threed package hosts the public API surface, with Scene, Node, and Entity forming the core scene graph hierarchy."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "identity:repository",
        "public_symbol:com",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:com",
      "text": "The top-level com namespace exposes the com.aspose package as its primary public API surface."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "identity:repository",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:com.aspose",
      "text": "The com.aspose namespace provides the aspose.threed module, which contains the 3D scene graph and I/O functionality."
    },
    {
      "fact_ids": [
        "identity:repository",
        "public_symbol:com.aspose.threed"
      ],
      "section": "api_reference",
      "slot": "hub:public_symbol:com.aspose.threed",
      "text": "The com.aspose.threed namespace hosts the Scene class, which loads geometry via Scene.fromFile with automatic format detection, exposes the scene graph through getRootNode, and writes output via Scene.save."
    },
